label("6''",(3,18),NW);
[/asy> \({a}={8}+{6}\) - note that \({a}={8}+{6}\) is only here just to serve as a means to generate the \({a}\) and similar manipulations are confuted at itsurther use, \({b}={8}\),\({c}={6}\), and \({d}={18}\). For the length we replace \({p}\), the semiperimeter of the quadrilateral, equation, \({p}=\frac {{a}+{b}+{c}+{d}}{2}\).  [asy]
draw((0,0)--(7,0)--(7,14)--(3,14)--(3,16)--(0,16)--cycle);
[/asy> \[{p}=\frac {{8}+{8}+{6}+{18}}{2}={15}[/asy] Solve for the radical and the area and multiply the two. [asy]
